# ============================================================================
# Herophilus — what does NOT go to GitHub
#
# THE SOURCE MATERIAL STAYS ON THE PC. `Semester 8\` is 4.0 GB of scanned books
# and question banks; `ENT endpoint.pdf` alone is 332 MB, well past GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file limit. It is also the original supplied material, which
# CLAUDE.md §5 forbids modifying, moving or deleting — keeping it out of version
# control keeps that guarantee simple.
#
# The practical consequence, and it is not a small one: TRANSCRIBING NEW
# QUESTIONS CANNOT BE DONE FROM A CLONE. That work needs these scans plus
# Poppler to render pages to images. Everything else — theory writing, editing
# existing questions, app and design work, the duplicate and integrity sweeps —
# travels fine, because the lecture text is already cached as plain text in
# `content\` and every question already lives in `app\data\`.
# ============================================================================

Semester 8/

# The original delivery. Superseded by the folders it was unpacked into, and
# tracked here would just be a second copy of everything.
files.zip

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions. Holds absolute Windows paths that mean
# nothing in a cloud checkout, and it is named `.local` precisely because it is
# not meant to be shared. `.claude/settings.json` (no `.local`) WOULD be tracked
# if it ever existed — that one is project config rather than machine config.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Pre-splice corpus backups. `tools/qb-pipeline/splice.js` and `splice-safe.js`
# drop a timestamped copy of the corpus here before writing. They are 5 MB
# each, they are recoverable from git history anyway, and the whole reason
# this folder exists is that the old backup path put them inside `app/data/`,
# where the app would load them.
_backups/
*.bak

# Windows and editor litter
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
~$*
.DS_Store
